"F06761"	"tests/PhotoReview.Core.Tests/Catalog/GenerationClockTests.cs"	"8"	"21"	"MethodDeclaration"	"GenerationClockTests.[Theory] [InlineData(0, 0, 0)] [InlineData(12, 34, 56)] public void Constructor_InitializesGenerationsToSpecifiedValues(long navigation, long folder, long interaction)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Checks all three explicit counters and IsCurrent for zero/nonzero constructor values; does not require thread-affine initialization. Mutation checks not run. BODY: [Theory] [InlineData(0, 0, 0)] [InlineData(12, 34, 56)] public void Constructor_InitializesGenerationsToSpecifiedValues(long navigation, long folder, long interaction) { var clock = new GenerationClock(initialNavigation: navigation, initialFolder: folder, initialInteraction: interaction); Assert.Equal(navigation, clock.CurrentNavigation); Assert.Equal(folder, clock.CurrentFolder); Assert.Equal(interaction, clock.CurrentInteraction); Assert.True(clock.IsNavigationCurrent(navigation)); Assert.True(clock.IsFolderCurrent(folder)); Assert.True(clock.IsInteractionCurrent(interaction)); }"
"F06762"	"tests/PhotoReview.Core.Tests/Catalog/GenerationClockTests.cs"	"25"	"44"	"MethodDeclaration"	"GenerationClockTests.[Theory] [InlineData(Generation.Navigation)] [InlineData(Generation.Folder)] [InlineData(Generation.Interaction)] public void Next_IncrementsMonotonicallyAndUpdatesCurrent(Generation generation)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Each counter twice must return1/2, update Current and reject old token; exact ordering protects increment and generation guard. Mutation checks not run. BODY: [Theory] [InlineData(Generation.Navigation)] [InlineData(Generation.Folder)] [InlineData(Generation.Interaction)] public void Next_IncrementsMonotonicallyAndUpdatesCurrent(Generation generation) { var clock = new GenerationClock(); var t1 = Next(clock, generation); Assert.Equal(1, t1); Assert.Equal(1, Current(clock, generation)); Assert.True(IsCurrent(clock, generation, 1)); Assert.False(IsCurrent(clock, generation, 0)); var t2 = Next(clock, generation); Assert.Equal(2, t2); Assert.Equal(2, Current(clock, generation)); Assert.True(IsCurrent(clock, generation, 2)); Assert.False(IsCurrent(clock, generation, 1)); }"
"F06763"	"tests/PhotoReview.Core.Tests/Catalog/GenerationClockTests.cs"	"46"	"51"	"MethodDeclaration"	"GenerationClockTests.private static long Next(GenerationClock clock, Generation generation)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Helper/lambda body inspected in complete test context: exact captured callback/value expression below supplies fixture or guarded call; has no independent test oracle. Mutation checks not run. BODY: private static long Next(GenerationClock clock, Generation generation) => generation switch { Generation.Navigation => clock.NextNavigation(), Generation.Folder => clock.NextFolder(), _ => clock.NextInteraction(), };"
"F06764"	"tests/PhotoReview.Core.Tests/Catalog/GenerationClockTests.cs"	"53"	"58"	"MethodDeclaration"	"GenerationClockTests.private static long Current(GenerationClock clock, Generation generation)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Helper/lambda body inspected in complete test context: exact captured callback/value expression below supplies fixture or guarded call; has no independent test oracle. Mutation checks not run. BODY: private static long Current(GenerationClock clock, Generation generation) => generation switch { Generation.Navigation => clock.CurrentNavigation, Generation.Folder => clock.CurrentFolder, _ => clock.CurrentInteraction, };"
"F06765"	"tests/PhotoReview.Core.Tests/Catalog/GenerationClockTests.cs"	"60"	"65"	"MethodDeclaration"	"GenerationClockTests.private static bool IsCurrent(GenerationClock clock, Generation generation, long value)"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Helper/lambda body inspected in complete test context: exact captured callback/value expression below supplies fixture or guarded call; has no independent test oracle. Mutation checks not run. BODY: private static bool IsCurrent(GenerationClock clock, Generation generation, long value) => generation switch { Generation.Navigation => clock.IsNavigationCurrent(value), Generation.Folder => clock.IsFolderCurrent(value), _ => clock.IsInteractionCurrent(value), };"
"F06766"	"tests/PhotoReview.Core.Tests/Catalog/GenerationClockTests.cs"	"67"	"83"	"MethodDeclaration"	"GenerationClockTests.[Fact] public void StopForAction_IncrementsAllThreeCountersSimultaneously()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Post-call values/current-stale flags protect all counters advancing. Despite name, no mid-call observer checks atomic simultaneous publication. Mutation checks not run. BODY: [Fact] public void StopForAction_IncrementsAllThreeCountersSimultaneously() { var clock = new GenerationClock(5, 10, 15); clock.StopForAction(); Assert.Equal(6, clock.CurrentNavigation); Assert.Equal(11, clock.CurrentFolder); Assert.Equal(16, clock.CurrentInteraction); Assert.True(clock.IsNavigationCurrent(6)); Assert.True(clock.IsFolderCurrent(11)); Assert.True(clock.IsInteractionCurrent(16)); Assert.False(clock.IsNavigationCurrent(5)); Assert.False(clock.IsFolderCurrent(10)); Assert.False(clock.IsInteractionCurrent(15)); }"
"F06767"	"tests/PhotoReview.Core.Tests/Catalog/GenerationClockTests.cs"	"85"	"104"	"MethodDeclaration"	"GenerationClockTests.[Fact] public void ConcurrentIncrements_AreThreadSafeAndAccurate()"	"STATIC-ONLY"	"Parallel10000 increments on each counter with exact final values/current tokens detect lost increments; no cross-counter atomic snapshot claim. Mutation checks not run. BODY: [Fact] public void ConcurrentIncrements_AreThreadSafeAndAccurate() { var clock = new GenerationClock(); const int iterations = 10_000; Parallel.For(0, iterations, _ => { clock.NextNavigation(); clock.NextFolder(); clock.NextInteraction(); }); Assert.Equal(iterations, clock.CurrentNavigation); Assert.Equal(iterations, clock.CurrentFolder); Assert.Equal(iterations, clock.CurrentInteraction); Assert.True(clock.IsNavigationCurrent(iterations)); Assert.True(clock.IsFolderCurrent(iterations)); Assert.True(clock.IsInteractionCurrent(iterations)); }"
